From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:11:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] client: the light curve is set before the terrain loads

The curve that turns light levels into brightness was set as the game loop started. Since the
loading screen waits for the terrain (loading_terrain_radius), the meshes of the blocks around
the player are made before that, and until then the curve's table is all zeros: they came out
black but for what gives light of its own, torches drawn on dark walls. Meshes made once the game
ran were right, so the dark stayed until a block there changed and was meshed again, a dig or a
placed node, or the world was opened again.

Found on the owner's console in a dungeon room at a fixed time of day: the same join was dark
with the terrain wait and lit without it; the blocks, their light and the draw list were the
same in both, and meshing every block again at the end of the wait made it lit. The two commits
before this one came from an earlier reading of the same bug: blocks are not dropped as far at
the join, but they do no harm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/client/game.cpp b/src/client/game.cpp
index 81b2f54ea..91e744d10 100644
--- a/src/client/game.cpp
+++ b/src/client/game.cpp
@@ -458,6 +458,8 @@ bool Game::startup(volatile std::sig_atomic_t *kill,
 	m_first_loop_after_window_activation = true;
 
 	g_client_translations->clear();
+	// before any block mesh: loadTerrain() makes them before the game runs
+	set_light_curve(g_settings->getFloat("display_gamma"));
 
 	// with the terrain to wait for (a local game, see loadTerrain), the steps before it fill the first 60 %
 	if (g_settings->getS16("loading_terrain_radius") > 0 && start_data.address.empty())
@@ -500,8 +502,6 @@ void Game::run()
 
 	draw_times.reset();
 
-	set_light_curve(g_settings->getFloat("display_gamma"));
-
 	m_touch_simulate_aux1 = g_settings->getBool("fast_move")
 			&& client->checkPrivilege("fast");
 
